## 8. If you redistribute a project generated from this framework

CC BY-SA 4.0 Section 3(a) requires attribution to travel with the material
when you Share it — including in modified/rendered form (e.g. a project
tree produced by `copier copy`/`harness-install.sh`). **Implemented in
H5/B2:** every rendered project now receives its own root-level `NOTICE`
(from `templates/NOTICE.jinja`), generated unconditionally because
`.harness/lib/docs_wiki_lint.py`, `ref_integrity.py`, and `scan_project.py`
are always installed and carry the guto-wiki/Understand-Anything provenance;
the file adds a second section (Trail of Bits' ten skills, `diataxis`, and
the three learnhouse-internal skills) only when `use_claude=true`, matching
exactly what actually lands in `.claude/skills/`. `harness-install.sh`
needed no code change for this: the target's `NOTICE` is not one of the four
"sensitive" merge-tracked files, so it flows through the same generic
create/overwrite path as every other framework-owned file. This project's
own `NOTICE` (the one you're reading) is the full, unabridged, always-current
version; the generated one is the scoped summary that ships downstream —
if you edit which skills are included in a fork of this framework, keep
`templates/NOTICE.jinja` in sync (there is no test enforcing that sync yet;
see `docs/manual/15-limitacoes-conhecidas.md` item 14).
